---
const claudeCodeConfig = `{
  "mcpServers": {
    "browxai": {
      "command": "browxai"
    }
  }
}`;

const codexToml = `[mcp_servers.browxai]
command = "browxai"`;

const codexRemoteToml = `[mcp_servers.browxai]
url = "https://<relay-host>/mcp"
bearer_token_env_var = "BROWXAI_RELAY_TOKEN"`;

const genericConfig = `{
  "command": "browxai",
  "args": []
}`;
---

<section class="harness-tabs" data-harness-tabs>
  <div class="harness-tab-list" role="tablist" aria-label="Harness setup">
    <button
      class="harness-tab"
      type="button"
      role="tab"
      id="harness-tab-claude-ai"
      aria-selected="true"
      aria-controls="harness-panel-claude-ai"
      data-harness-tab="claude-ai"
    >
      Claude.ai
    </button>
    <button
      class="harness-tab"
      type="button"
      role="tab"
      id="harness-tab-claude-code"
      aria-selected="false"
      aria-controls="harness-panel-claude-code"
      data-harness-tab="claude-code"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      Claude Code
    </button>
    <button
      class="harness-tab"
      type="button"
      role="tab"
      id="harness-tab-chatgpt"
      aria-selected="false"
      aria-controls="harness-panel-chatgpt"
      data-harness-tab="chatgpt"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      ChatGPT
    </button>
    <button
      class="harness-tab"
      type="button"
      role="tab"
      id="harness-tab-codex"
      aria-selected="false"
      aria-controls="harness-panel-codex"
      data-harness-tab="codex"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      Codex
    </button>
    <button
      class="harness-tab"
      type="button"
      role="tab"
      id="harness-tab-generic"
      aria-selected="false"
      aria-controls="harness-panel-generic"
      data-harness-tab="generic"
      tabindex="-1"
    >
      Generic MCP
    </button>
  </div>

  <div
    class="harness-panel"
    role="tabpanel"
    id="harness-panel-claude-ai"
    aria-labelledby="harness-tab-claude-ai"
    data-harness-panel="claude-ai"
  >
    <h3>Claude.ai, Claude Cowork, and Claude Desktop sandboxed access</h3>
    <p>
      These are remote MCP surfaces. They cannot launch a local stdio command on your machine, so
      use a relay-provided HTTPS MCP endpoint connected to a browxai host running on your hardware.
    </p>
    <pre><code>MCP endpoint: https://&lt;relay-host&gt;/mcp
Transport: Streamable HTTP
Authentication: relay-provided bearer token or OAuth flow</code></pre>
    <p>
      Do not paste a local <code>.mcp.json</code> command into Claude.ai. The local browser and
      browxai process stay on your hardware; the relay only gives Claude a reachable MCP endpoint.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div
    class="harness-panel"
    role="tabpanel"
    id="harness-panel-claude-code"
    aria-labelledby="harness-tab-claude-code"
    data-harness-panel="claude-code"
    hidden
  >
    <h3>Claude Code</h3>
    <p>
      Preferred path: add the browxai repo as a custom Claude Code plugin marketplace, then
      install the <code>browxai</code> plugin from marketplace <code>browxai</code>.
    </p>
    <pre><code class="language-text">/plugin marketplace add https://github.com/kalebteccom/browxai.git
/plugin install browxai@browxai</code></pre>
    <p>
      The plugin bundles the <code>driving-browxai</code> skill and a local stdio MCP server config
      that invokes <code>browxai</code> from <code>PATH</code>. It does not install browsers or
      enable off-by-default capabilities.
    </p>
    <p>Manual fallback: add browxai to your project MCP config:</p>
    <pre><code class="language-jsonc">{claudeCodeConfig}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Restart Claude Code and check <code>/mcp</code>. For Claude Code cloud or any sandboxed
      Claude surface that cannot run your local process, use the remote MCP endpoint from your relay
      instead of the local command.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div
    class="harness-panel"
    role="tabpanel"
    id="harness-panel-chatgpt"
    aria-labelledby="harness-tab-chatgpt"
    data-harness-panel="chatgpt"
    hidden
  >
    <h3>ChatGPT</h3>
    <p>ChatGPT uses remote MCP connectors. Configure it with the HTTPS MCP endpoint provided by your relay:</p>
    <pre><code>Server URL: https://&lt;relay-host&gt;/mcp
Authentication: relay-provided bearer token or OAuth flow</code></pre>
    <p>
      Installing the local package alone is not enough for ChatGPT because ChatGPT cannot reach a
      stdio server on your machine. The relay must be paired to your local browxai/browser host.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div
    class="harness-panel"
    role="tabpanel"
    id="harness-panel-codex"
    aria-labelledby="harness-tab-codex"
    data-harness-panel="codex"
    hidden
  >
    <h3>Codex</h3>
    <p>
      Preferred path: add the browxai repo as a Codex plugin marketplace, then install the
      <code>browxai</code> plugin from the Codex plugin directory.
    </p>
    <pre><code class="language-bash">codex plugin marketplace add kalebteccom/browxai</code></pre>
    <p>
      The repo marketplace lives at <code>.agents/plugins/marketplace.json</code>. The plugin
      bundles the <code>driving-browxai</code> skill and a local stdio MCP server config that
      invokes <code>browxai</code> from <code>PATH</code>.
    </p>
    <p>Manual fallback: register browxai as a stdio MCP server:</p>
    <pre><code class="language-bash">codex mcp add browxai -- browxai</code></pre>
    <p>Equivalent <code>config.toml</code>:</p>
    <pre><code class="language-toml">{codexToml}</code></pre>
    <p>Open <code>/mcp</code> in the Codex TUI to verify the server is connected.</p>
    <p>Codex also supports Streamable HTTP MCP. For a relay endpoint:</p>
    <pre><code class="language-toml">{codexRemoteToml}</code></pre>
  </div>

  <div
    class="harness-panel"
    role="tabpanel"
    id="harness-panel-generic"
    aria-labelledby="harness-tab-generic"
    data-harness-panel="generic"
    hidden
  >
    <h3>Generic MCP</h3>
    <p>For any MCP client that can launch local stdio servers, configure:</p>
    <pre><code class="language-json">{genericConfig}</code></pre>
    <p>
      For clients that run in the cloud or a sandbox, use the relay's Streamable HTTP endpoint
      instead. A local stdio command only works when the harness can execute commands on the same
      hardware where browxai and the browser run.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<script is:inline>
  for (const root of document.querySelectorAll("[data-harness-tabs]")) {
    const tabs = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll("[data-harness-tab]"));
    const panels = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll("[data-harness-panel]"));

    const activate = (tab) => {
      const selected = tab.getAttribute("data-harness-tab");
      for (const candidate of tabs) {
        const active = candidate === tab;
        candidate.setAttribute("aria-selected", active ? "true" : "false");
        candidate.tabIndex = active ? 0 : -1;
      }
      for (const panel of panels) {
        panel.hidden = panel.getAttribute("data-harness-panel") !== selected;
      }
      tab.focus();
    };

    for (const [index, tab] of tabs.entries()) {
      tab.addEventListener("click", () => activate(tab));
      tab.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
        if (event.key !== "ArrowRight" && event.key !== "ArrowLeft") return;
        event.preventDefault();
        const offset = event.key === "ArrowRight" ? 1 : -1;
        const next = tabs[(index + offset + tabs.length) % tabs.length];
        activate(next);
      });
    }
  }
</script>

<style>
  .harness-tabs {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 1.75rem;
  }

  .harness-tab-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
  }

  .harness-tab {
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-bottom: 0;
    border-radius: 0.5rem 0.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0.55rem 0.8rem;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
    font: inherit;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .harness-tab:hover,
  .harness-tab:focus-visible {
    color: var(--sl-color-text);
    background: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
  }

  .harness-tab[aria-selected="true"] {
    border-color: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    background: var(--sl-color-bg);
    color: var(--sl-color-accent-high);
    position: relative;
    top: 1px;
  }

  .harness-panel {
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    border-top: 0;
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .harness-panel[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .harness-panel h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .harness-panel pre {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.85rem;
    background: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-code-sm);
  }

  .harness-panel p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
